1
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:08,110
No living creature was
harmed during the filming.

2
00:02:08,899 --> 00:02:14,259
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:23,295 --> 00:02:25,365
If they know we are here...

4
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:28,430
they'll go to Turgut Bey for it.

5
00:02:28,762 --> 00:02:30,892
There were soldiers running
up, my bey.

6
00:02:31,690 --> 00:02:35,590
Alps! For Turgut Bey!
Attack!

7
00:03:35,173 --> 00:03:37,573
Come on!

8
00:03:46,830 --> 00:03:49,060
You will pay for your betrayal!

9
00:03:49,227 --> 00:03:53,317
If I was with you,
that would be the real treason.

10
00:03:54,061 --> 00:03:56,451
Don't you still understand,
Rogatus?

11
00:03:56,614 --> 00:04:00,364
Against the weasels, all
wolves unite.

12
00:04:00,387 --> 00:04:02,097
They stand together!

13
00:04:07,901 --> 00:04:09,901
You won't get out of here!

14
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:11,710
Neither dead or alive.

15
00:04:12,064 --> 00:04:15,474
You should only survive
until Osman comes.

16
00:04:18,103 --> 00:04:21,284
Soldier! You did well by
watching him.

17
00:04:21,415 --> 00:04:24,555
I knew that Turks can't be trusted.

18
00:04:30,794 --> 00:04:32,744
We are here, Turgut Bey!

19
00:05:33,765 --> 00:05:35,313
Come here!

20
00:05:35,313 --> 00:05:37,315
There will be more soldiers, my bey.

21
00:05:37,315 --> 00:05:39,595
My bey, my bey, we need to leave!

22
00:05:39,595 --> 00:05:42,035
My bey, they are coming!

23
00:05:42,235 --> 00:05:45,575
Come on! My bey!

24
00:05:48,641 --> 00:05:50,161
My bey, this way!

25
00:06:02,395 --> 00:06:05,465
Move! Get them!

26
00:06:07,819 --> 00:06:09,439
Open it!

27
00:06:21,332 --> 00:06:23,022
Come on, alps!

28
00:06:31,734 --> 00:06:33,224
Crouch!

29
00:06:37,507 --> 00:06:39,107
Kill them!

30
00:06:40,451 --> 00:06:42,011
Crouch!

31
00:06:44,839 --> 00:06:46,389
Crouch!

32
00:06:50,545 --> 00:06:51,935
Crouch!

33
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:04,298
They are out of arrows!

34
00:07:05,276 --> 00:07:06,766
Open it!

35
00:07:07,033 --> 00:07:09,353
I won't leave the Turkmen kids!

36
00:07:09,837 --> 00:07:13,564
I'll return. For the kids and
your head, I'll return.

37
00:07:13,564 --> 00:07:15,214
Attack!

38
00:07:15,428 --> 00:07:17,128
Attack!

39
00:07:18,588 --> 00:07:19,898
Come on!

40
00:07:25,372 --> 00:07:29,132
They are going to the secret passage!

41
00:07:36,007 --> 00:07:37,487
Come on!

42
00:07:50,034 --> 00:07:52,614
Break it! Break it!

43
00:08:12,326 --> 00:08:13,876
Open it!

44
00:08:13,877 --> 00:08:15,287
Hit it!

45
00:08:15,723 --> 00:08:17,022
Come on, alps!

46
00:08:17,022 --> 00:08:19,402
Open it!

47
00:08:24,348 --> 00:08:26,068
Cerkutay!

48
00:08:28,136 --> 00:08:29,376
Come on!

49
00:08:29,376 --> 00:08:30,582
Hold it, brother!

50
00:08:30,582 --> 00:08:32,692
Open this! Open it!

51
00:08:34,922 --> 00:08:36,312
Allahu Akbar.

52
00:08:39,578 --> 00:08:41,628
Come on. Mashalah.
Come on.

53
00:08:43,049 --> 00:08:44,900
Open it!

54
00:08:46,246 --> 00:08:48,136
Open it!

55
00:08:50,458 --> 00:08:52,648
Move out! Move out!

56
00:09:09,864 --> 00:09:11,684
We couldn't get the kids.

57
00:09:11,764 --> 00:09:13,366
What will we do, Osman Bey?

58
00:09:13,366 --> 00:09:16,596
My warriors are nimble.
They left marks.

59
00:09:16,970 --> 00:09:18,940
They are going to the abbey.

60
00:09:19,156 --> 00:09:20,856
So will we.

61
00:09:20,945 --> 00:09:23,625
But not now. There is time.

62
00:09:24,032 --> 00:09:25,822
Return to your tribe.

63
00:09:26,191 --> 00:09:29,341
So be it.

64
00:09:34,189 --> 00:09:38,949
Osman even knows the secret
passages in my castle!

65
00:09:39,544 --> 00:09:41,894
And what are you doing?

66
00:09:44,559 --> 00:09:46,389
What are you doing?

67
00:09:48,086 --> 00:09:50,646
You should thank God that
he couldn't take the kids.

68
00:09:51,295 --> 00:09:56,025
Otherwise, I would break every
one of your skulls...

69
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,660
one by one.

70
00:10:05,291 --> 00:10:09,641
I sent Bahadır after Gökçe.
I want you to ask the women.

71
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:13,560
There surely be something to follow.

72
00:10:14,271 --> 00:10:16,119
They are shrewd.

73
00:10:16,119 --> 00:10:18,419
They must've seen something.

74
00:10:18,459 --> 00:10:20,319
Don't worry.

75
00:10:20,614 --> 00:10:22,722
I trust you, Aygül.

76
00:10:22,722 --> 00:10:25,512
Together, we'll find the traitor.

77
00:10:25,676 --> 00:10:27,596
Inshallah.

78
00:10:30,086 --> 00:10:34,006
When did the Kayı tribe ever
held a traitor?

79
00:10:34,067 --> 00:10:35,757
Malhun Hatun.

80
00:10:37,990 --> 00:10:40,370
It will be revealed.

81
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:50,490
Bala.

82
00:10:51,742 --> 00:10:53,712
Ayşe told me.

83
00:10:54,369 --> 00:10:57,619
You didn't eat anything.

84
00:10:57,866 --> 00:11:00,206
Don't be like this, my girl.

85
00:11:04,417 --> 00:11:06,227
I'm hurt, mother.

86
00:11:08,302 --> 00:11:10,552
Gonca flied away.

87
00:11:11,224 --> 00:11:13,524
Ahmed is on the heathens' hands.

88
00:11:13,850 --> 00:11:15,795
Osman didn't return.

89
00:11:15,795 --> 00:11:17,615
He will.

90
00:11:17,674 --> 00:11:19,774
Of course, he will!

91
00:11:19,858 --> 00:11:22,938
He will return with Ahmed!

92
00:11:23,228 --> 00:11:25,078
Inshallah, mother.

93
00:11:25,078 --> 00:11:26,808
Inshallah.

94
00:11:34,792 --> 00:11:36,472
Osman!

95
00:11:45,929 --> 00:11:48,079
Don't be grieved.

96
00:11:48,316 --> 00:11:50,176
Our warriors left tracks.

97
00:11:53,098 --> 00:11:55,588
We know where are they taken to.

98
00:11:56,499 --> 00:11:58,072
Thank Allah.

99
00:11:58,072 --> 00:12:00,402
Mashallah to my lions.

100
00:12:00,442 --> 00:12:02,232
Where are they, Osman Bey?

101
00:12:02,324 --> 00:12:04,334
They are taken to Hristo Abbey, brother.

102
00:12:04,547 --> 00:12:06,687
Cerkutay must be there already.

103
00:12:06,868 --> 00:12:09,908
After he scouts the place,
we'll take our children back.

104
00:12:16,103 --> 00:12:18,803
Hristo Abbey

105
00:12:28,586 --> 00:12:31,116
The Kayı's warriors.

106
00:12:35,190 --> 00:12:37,040
We'll take you back.

107
00:12:37,981 --> 00:12:40,701
We won't leave you in the enemy's hands.

108
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:01,680
Get inside.

109
00:13:16,225 --> 00:13:19,215
You all will be good Christians.

110
00:13:22,070 --> 00:13:23,830
You heathens!

111
00:13:24,698 --> 00:13:26,888
Our hearts are filled with faith!

112
00:13:27,470 --> 00:13:29,220
We don't bow down.

113
00:13:30,785 --> 00:13:33,115
Let's start with your look.

114
00:13:34,795 --> 00:13:37,435
Behave, my good children.
Behave.

115
00:13:49,156 --> 00:13:52,746
Don't worry. Osman Bey will save us.

116
00:13:54,827 --> 00:13:57,017
He knows we are here.

117
00:13:57,114 --> 00:13:59,314
I left tracks on the dungeon.

118
00:14:04,409 --> 00:14:06,519
Don't let your eyes get wet.

119
00:14:08,099 --> 00:14:13,039
We'll take Ahmed and our children
from their hands.

120
00:14:13,675 --> 00:14:15,595
Don't worry.

121
00:14:15,837 --> 00:14:18,327
You don't sharpen your sword
for nothing.

122
00:14:18,489 --> 00:14:20,089
Of course, we will.

123
00:14:20,695 --> 00:14:22,925
We'll take our children...

124
00:14:23,362 --> 00:14:26,012
and their heads.

125
00:14:29,244 --> 00:14:31,194
Be at ease.

126
00:14:34,438 --> 00:14:36,418
May I enter, my bey?

127
00:14:36,529 --> 00:14:38,359
Come.

128
00:14:47,678 --> 00:14:50,618
I've talked to the women, my bey.
They are content.

129
00:14:50,706 --> 00:14:53,546
They are praying in your name.
They await good news.

130
00:14:56,038 --> 00:14:57,598
Soon.

131
00:14:57,980 --> 00:15:00,710
They will reunite with their children.

132
00:15:03,388 --> 00:15:05,828
May I enter, my bey?

133
00:15:06,274 --> 00:15:08,184
Come, Cerkutay.

134
00:15:13,955 --> 00:15:17,315
My bey, the Ahmed's marks
proved right.

135
00:15:17,346 --> 00:15:19,586
They are in the abbey.

136
00:15:23,151 --> 00:15:25,111
Mashallah.

137
00:15:26,568 --> 00:15:28,358
Tell the mothers.

138
00:15:28,397 --> 00:15:31,597
It's time they reunite with
their children.

139
00:16:11,992 --> 00:16:14,672
Heathens finally touched
our children.

140
00:16:16,297 --> 00:16:19,267
They are out of control, Davud Agha.

141
00:16:24,113 --> 00:16:25,523
Out of control.

142
00:16:27,362 --> 00:16:29,612
A great battle will take place.

143
00:16:29,850 --> 00:16:31,280
We'll see.

144
00:16:31,581 --> 00:16:36,011
Valiants show themselves
in battle.

145
00:16:38,126 --> 00:16:41,886
Weapons, Gündüz Bey.
We need more weapons.

146
00:16:45,965 --> 00:16:50,645
Davud Agha, if we fight
a great battle...

147
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:53,140
do you say that we don't
have enough weapons?

148
00:16:53,141 --> 00:16:56,161
Not at all, my bey.
We have weapons.

149
00:16:56,564 --> 00:17:00,854
But if you say a great battle,
weapons won't be enough.

150
00:17:01,492 --> 00:17:03,352
We need more weapons.

151
00:17:06,815 --> 00:17:08,464
You are right.

152
00:17:11,262 --> 00:17:13,423
With the name of Allah.

153
00:17:18,368 --> 00:17:20,489
We'll find a way.

154
00:17:22,828 --> 00:17:24,848
We will.

155
00:17:26,273 --> 00:17:27,753
We will.

156
00:17:31,573 --> 00:17:34,753
Aya Yorgi Abbey

157
00:18:08,568 --> 00:18:11,178
You won't change us.

158
00:18:13,396 --> 00:18:15,316
The children are inside.

159
00:18:15,809 --> 00:18:18,209
They are protecting them with
soldiers.

160
00:18:19,753 --> 00:18:22,267
The place has two doors.

161
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:24,847
And both entrances are protected
by two soldiers each.

162
00:18:26,253 --> 00:18:28,903
Five soldiers are patrolling the
yard.

163
00:18:29,759 --> 00:18:32,049
When we break the gate and
get inside...

164
00:18:32,271 --> 00:18:35,201
Turgut Bey, you will attack
the yard.

165
00:18:37,221 --> 00:18:39,081
I sent Aykut earlier.

166
00:18:39,734 --> 00:18:43,134
He'll let us know if there are
any soldiers other than the monks inside.

167
00:18:44,008 --> 00:18:46,228
The rest will be dealt with by
our swords.

168
00:18:47,561 --> 00:18:51,581
But don't forget that we have
children in there.

169
00:18:52,065 --> 00:18:54,115
Remember that while using
your weapons.

170
00:18:58,339 --> 00:18:59,859
Alps!

171
00:19:00,075 --> 00:19:01,845
To the horses!

172
00:19:22,675 --> 00:19:24,055
Osman!

173
00:19:27,729 --> 00:19:30,719
Did you think that I would
give them to you that easily?

174
00:19:40,725 --> 00:19:42,665
He couldn't get the kids.

175
00:20:01,264 --> 00:20:02,814
Damn it!

176
00:20:03,342 --> 00:20:06,562
Osman knows the location of
the kids!

177
00:20:09,684 --> 00:20:12,384
You! Leave at once!

178
00:20:12,384 --> 00:20:16,084
The children shouldn't be taken to
Hristo Abbey but to Aya Yorgi Abbey!

179
00:20:16,084 --> 00:20:17,484
Move!

180
00:20:17,771 --> 00:20:20,281
Soldiers! Get ready.

181
00:20:20,926 --> 00:20:24,686
Nikola, Kosses and I...

182
00:20:26,138 --> 00:20:27,908
will greet Osman.

183
00:20:29,160 --> 00:20:34,280
But firstly, let's find some Turkish
clothing for the Christian kids.

184
00:20:35,536 --> 00:20:38,846
Osman will think that they
are Turkish.

185
00:20:41,241 --> 00:20:43,901
What are you waiting for?

186
00:20:57,142 --> 00:20:59,972
You can't survive every ambush, Osman Bey.

187
00:21:00,150 --> 00:21:02,230
It's over now!

188
00:21:09,815 --> 00:21:11,675
Attack!

189
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:23,350
Archers!

190
00:22:24,817 --> 00:22:26,435
To the hill!

191
00:22:26,435 --> 00:22:28,265
Don't let them pass!

192
00:22:43,148 --> 00:22:45,218
Come on!

193
00:22:49,947 --> 00:22:53,607
What happened? Did you get
hunted in your hunt?

194
00:23:00,069 --> 00:23:02,619
You will run away like this!

195
00:23:04,011 --> 00:23:07,331
A wolf! You can't bite the lion!

196
00:23:07,764 --> 00:23:11,154
But I must give it to him.
He cares about children.

197
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:13,850
He fell into the trap without
even thinking.

198
00:23:14,157 --> 00:23:16,239
But he couldn't get the children.

199
00:23:16,239 --> 00:23:19,909
The only thing he got is
a defeat!

200
00:23:23,199 --> 00:23:24,589
Now...

201
00:23:25,645 --> 00:23:29,365
we can visit the little Turks
in their new home!

202
00:23:31,391 --> 00:23:38,434
Long live the Empire!

203
00:24:51,271 --> 00:24:52,851
Aytekin?

204
00:24:56,453 --> 00:24:58,143
My son...

205
00:25:04,489 --> 00:25:06,169
Ahmed...
No...

206
00:25:12,900 --> 00:25:14,560
No...

207
00:25:18,693 --> 00:25:21,553
My bey...
Our children...

208
00:25:23,260 --> 00:25:26,570
Osman Bey, you subjugated the
whole world but...

209
00:25:26,570 --> 00:25:29,570
you couldn't bring
our children back!

210
00:26:26,639 --> 00:26:28,459
Don't you see?

211
00:26:28,647 --> 00:26:32,185
They can't stand in our way
because of fear!

212
00:26:32,265 --> 00:26:34,905
So that they go after our children!

213
00:26:38,295 --> 00:26:43,515
With Allah's help,
Osman Bey will bring our children back!

214
00:26:44,465 --> 00:26:46,424
Inshallah.

215
00:26:46,424 --> 00:26:48,854
You are Kayı women!

216
00:26:50,126 --> 00:26:52,426
Don't lower your heads!

217
00:26:59,516 --> 00:27:00,966
Come on.

218
00:27:03,798 --> 00:27:05,118
Come on, my girl.

219
00:27:05,748 --> 00:27:07,468
We'll be strong.

220
00:27:09,478 --> 00:27:12,128
Don't.
Come on.

221
00:27:23,333 --> 00:27:24,903
Come on.

222
00:29:20,354 --> 00:29:22,124
O' my Allah!

223
00:29:24,701 --> 00:29:27,421
Give me strenght...

224
00:29:29,511 --> 00:29:31,711
to take my children back!

225
00:29:33,511 --> 00:29:35,571
To the mothers
who are in pain...

226
00:29:37,290 --> 00:29:39,850
I need to bring their
children back...

227
00:29:41,209 --> 00:29:43,439
help me!

228
00:29:48,069 --> 00:29:50,059
O' my Allah!

229
00:29:50,457 --> 00:29:53,007
Answer my prayers!

230
00:29:56,002 --> 00:29:57,862
Amin, my Allah!

231
00:30:07,039 --> 00:30:10,724
You are my witness, Mother Selcan.
I wanted...

232
00:30:10,724 --> 00:30:13,483
a baby, a child so eagerly.

233
00:30:13,483 --> 00:30:16,404
Allah heard my prayers and gave him to me.

234
00:30:16,404 --> 00:30:20,336
But where is my baby now? I can't live
without him, Mother Selcan.

235
00:30:20,686 --> 00:30:23,196
Aya Yorgi Monastery

236
00:30:31,631 --> 00:30:34,181
You know how to do this
very well, Rogatus.

237
00:30:36,128 --> 00:30:39,678
You little monks.

238
00:30:41,656 --> 00:30:43,236
You.

239
00:30:43,320 --> 00:30:44,790
Tell me.

240
00:30:44,873 --> 00:30:48,153
Which of the four gospels do
you like the most?

241
00:30:48,476 --> 00:30:51,342
If you ask me, I'd prefer
the Gospel of Luke.

242
00:30:51,342 --> 00:30:54,032
-What about you?
-Our book is one.

243
00:30:57,841 --> 00:31:00,311
I don't worship what you worship.

244
00:31:05,464 --> 00:31:08,964
If the reason for this arrogance
is Osman...

245
00:31:10,006 --> 00:31:11,766
don't trust him that much.

246
00:31:12,610 --> 00:31:15,930
I found the trace you left
in that dungeon.

247
00:31:17,934 --> 00:31:21,904
We set a trap for Osman who
you love very much.

248
00:31:22,644 --> 00:31:24,955
You are lying!

249
00:31:28,578 --> 00:31:32,138
Osman is defeated, Alexander.

250
00:31:32,484 --> 00:31:34,344
We defeated him.

251
00:31:49,905 --> 00:31:52,835
Osman will never be able
to get the children.

252
00:31:53,550 --> 00:31:57,360
But he returned from Nicaea with
a good agreement.

253
00:31:57,408 --> 00:32:00,828
What does it matter? If Söğüt will be
on fire, what does it matter?

254
00:32:01,030 --> 00:32:02,490
Exactly.

255
00:32:02,490 --> 00:32:07,260
All of their trade resources, families
and traders are in Söğüt.

256
00:32:07,719 --> 00:32:12,079
If Söğüt burns, none of those
agreements mean anything.

257
00:32:12,168 --> 00:32:14,156
Before everything, Söğüt will be on fire.

258
00:32:14,156 --> 00:32:18,906
It will burn in such a way that its flames
will be visible from Constantinople.

259
00:32:18,906 --> 00:32:21,203
But it's not enough for it just to burn.

260
00:32:21,203 --> 00:32:25,021
After Priest Gregorious has
done his duty...

261
00:32:25,021 --> 00:32:29,281
we will be standing by to enter Söğüt
with our own soldiers.

262
00:32:30,241 --> 00:32:33,181
Fire can rule everything.

263
00:32:34,380 --> 00:32:36,730
We will rule Osman.

264
00:32:38,956 --> 00:32:41,576
Now, if you will excuse me...

265
00:32:41,810 --> 00:32:44,440
we have a very big fire to start.

266
00:32:45,929 --> 00:32:51,139
I hope these little monks choose their
favorite gospel as soon as possible.

267
00:32:53,730 --> 00:32:55,260
See you later.

268
00:33:03,946 --> 00:33:07,716
We will take our children from
their hands sooner or later.

269
00:33:08,268 --> 00:33:10,838
Is there any trace of that traitor...

270
00:33:11,671 --> 00:33:13,341
who caused so much trouble?

271
00:33:13,341 --> 00:33:15,991
There is nothing clear yet, my Bey.

272
00:33:16,270 --> 00:33:18,830
But we have our eyes on Gökçe.

273
00:33:19,391 --> 00:33:24,381
Like the fruit-bearing tree, of course,
our tribe will have also rotten fruits.

274
00:33:25,294 --> 00:33:30,594
But before this rot gets to the root and
tree, it must be cut as soon as possible.

275
00:33:32,235 --> 00:33:35,145
Find who hides the traitor as
soon as possible also.

276
00:33:53,343 --> 00:33:55,723
Orhan misses his father.

277
00:34:15,013 --> 00:34:17,243
The love for the child is a
beautiful...

278
00:34:18,070 --> 00:34:20,159
thing, isn't it?

279
00:34:25,536 --> 00:34:28,386
When so many people are
deprived of this...

280
00:34:31,827 --> 00:34:36,507
it is forbidden for me to smell or kiss
Orhan...

281
00:34:38,022 --> 00:34:40,081
without taking the children
of the Turks...

282
00:34:41,058 --> 00:34:43,618
from the hands of those infidels.

283
00:34:58,110 --> 00:35:00,220
Can I come in, my Bey?

284
00:35:01,064 --> 00:35:02,594
Come.

285
00:35:09,203 --> 00:35:12,123
My Bey, Priest Gregorius wants to see you.

286
00:35:13,942 --> 00:35:15,662
Let him come.

287
00:35:19,513 --> 00:35:21,143
This way.

288
00:35:28,329 --> 00:35:30,279
Welcome, Priest Gregorius.

289
00:35:30,726 --> 00:35:33,986
I am very sorry for this terrible
event, Osman Bey.

290
00:35:35,641 --> 00:35:38,071
We are pleased that...

291
00:35:39,121 --> 00:35:40,991
you worry about our problems.

292
00:35:42,286 --> 00:35:45,146
I'm ready to do everything that I can
to save the children.

293
00:35:46,028 --> 00:35:47,888
I just wanted to say this.

294
00:35:49,228 --> 00:35:50,818
Thank you.

295
00:35:51,013 --> 00:35:53,313
But there is no need.

296
00:36:02,232 --> 00:36:04,735
As you wish, Osman Bey.

297
00:36:04,735 --> 00:36:09,625
But know that I'm ready to
help whenever you need me.

298
00:36:11,022 --> 00:36:12,722
Thank you.

299
00:36:14,386 --> 00:36:15,996
You can leave.

300
00:36:29,626 --> 00:36:31,226
The Priest.

301
00:36:32,083 --> 00:36:35,663
The Priest may come in handy as the
children are confined to the monastery.

302
00:36:36,413 --> 00:36:38,383
Why didn't you want, Osman Bey?

303
00:36:38,443 --> 00:36:40,583
We'll handle it by ourselves.

304
00:36:40,922 --> 00:36:44,912
We'll handle it by ourselves so that we
can be a big fish.

305
00:36:46,592 --> 00:36:48,932
I never trust the priests or monks when...

306
00:36:48,992 --> 00:36:51,432
the lives of children are at stake.

307
00:36:52,366 --> 00:36:54,096
We'll handle it by ourselves.

308
00:36:55,230 --> 00:36:57,900
I'll learn where Rogatus took the
children.

309
00:36:58,560 --> 00:37:03,050
We will take our children from their
hands before they get hurt.

310
00:37:06,693 --> 00:37:09,523
Didn't Osman's behavior seem
strange to you too, Andreas?

311
00:37:10,012 --> 00:37:13,962
I don't like how he turned down
our offer of help.

312
00:37:14,649 --> 00:37:17,589
He was very affected by the
kidnapping of those children.

313
00:37:17,875 --> 00:37:19,855
What if he suspects us?

314
00:37:19,924 --> 00:37:22,313
What if he realized our purpose?

315
00:37:22,313 --> 00:37:24,883
If that were the case, he
wouldn't have left us alive.

316
00:37:24,883 --> 00:37:27,241
He would separate our
heads from our bodies.

317
00:37:28,560 --> 00:37:30,930
But we will be careful no matter what.

318
00:37:31,047 --> 00:37:33,927
The game in Söğüt will run smoothly.

319
00:37:36,980 --> 00:37:41,870
And Osman won't know anything
until he sees the rising flames.

320
00:37:47,293 --> 00:37:50,733
Aya Yorgi Monastery

321
00:38:01,014 --> 00:38:02,844
My Allah.

322
00:38:04,111 --> 00:38:06,761
I want Osman Bey to find us.

323
00:38:07,337 --> 00:38:10,007
That's why I left a trace.

324
00:38:10,992 --> 00:38:13,582
I wish I wouldn't do this.

325
00:38:15,636 --> 00:38:19,976
Osman Bey has fallen into
a trap because of me.

326
00:38:22,388 --> 00:38:24,318
Who will save us now?

327
00:38:27,283 --> 00:38:29,803
My Almighty Allah.

328
00:38:32,039 --> 00:38:35,709
I do not complain about any difficulties
that come to me from you.

329
00:38:37,442 --> 00:38:40,132
But my brothers are innocent.

330
00:38:43,305 --> 00:38:45,505
Osman Bey is innocent.

331
00:38:47,997 --> 00:38:51,827
My Allah, we have no remedy
other than you.

332
00:38:54,648 --> 00:38:57,668
We don't want help from
anyone other than you.

333
00:39:00,591 --> 00:39:03,011
Destroy all the traps.

334
00:39:03,733 --> 00:39:06,313
Save us from here.

335
00:39:07,434 --> 00:39:10,444
Grant us to live by our faith.

336
00:39:11,491 --> 00:39:13,171
Amen.

337
00:39:32,902 --> 00:39:35,362
Weapons are my only talent.

338
00:39:40,234 --> 00:39:42,184
Come on, play this qopuz.

339
00:39:43,354 --> 00:39:46,034
May the souls of veterans rest in peace.

340
00:39:47,737 --> 00:39:49,577
-Brother.
-Brother.

341
00:39:49,778 --> 00:39:51,518
Come on.

342
00:39:54,700 --> 00:39:57,810
Play the qopuz, brother.

343
00:40:00,179 --> 00:40:02,679
Healing the wounds in our hearts...

344
00:40:02,711 --> 00:40:05,431
is in your hands, brother.

345
00:40:08,917 --> 00:40:10,717
Alright.

346
00:41:01,893 --> 00:41:08,693
-Old Turkic song plays-

347
00:41:11,782 --> 00:41:16,662
-lyrics are in old Turkic-

348
00:43:56,297 --> 00:43:58,127
Bully for.

349
00:44:47,257 --> 00:44:50,837
O traveler, where is your journey to?

350
00:44:51,452 --> 00:44:53,422
To Kızılelma.

351
00:44:54,604 --> 00:44:56,834
What is the range?

352
00:44:57,367 --> 00:44:59,477
The death.

353
00:44:59,979 --> 00:45:01,906
For whom do you yearn?

354
00:45:01,906 --> 00:45:05,356
-For the Turkish land.
-Where is the Turkish land?

355
00:45:05,401 --> 00:45:07,501
The whole world.

356
00:45:07,703 --> 00:45:09,933
Let the whole world be your homeland.

357
00:45:11,103 --> 00:45:13,273
May the world be good to you.

358
00:45:13,717 --> 00:45:15,987
May your case be resulted in victory...

359
00:45:16,367 --> 00:45:17,957
Osman Bey

360
00:45:20,486 --> 00:45:22,746
Tell me what you heard from
Constantinople.

361
00:45:25,012 --> 00:45:28,732
As you wish, I learned the details.

362
00:45:29,509 --> 00:45:35,469
Rogatus wanted a priest from
Constantinople to educate the children.

363
00:45:36,908 --> 00:45:41,198
The Priest is going to the Aya Yorgi
Monastery in Kökhisar.

364
00:45:45,108 --> 00:45:48,388
The children are in there, Osman Bey.

365
00:45:50,329 --> 00:45:54,189
They took them there not
only to hide them...

366
00:45:55,588 --> 00:45:59,908
but to turn them from their way...

367
00:46:00,687 --> 00:46:04,697
and to make Turkish children Christians.

368
00:46:05,995 --> 00:46:08,815
But no one will be able to do this.

369
00:46:11,689 --> 00:46:15,539
Does the priest come with...

370
00:46:15,929 --> 00:46:17,769
a warrant or an edict?

371
00:46:20,311 --> 00:46:22,441
Yes, Osman Bey.

372
00:46:25,653 --> 00:46:28,763
Then prepare one for me too.

373
00:46:35,605 --> 00:46:36,992
The Castle of Harmankaya.

374
00:46:36,992 --> 00:46:40,192
You will be in Söğüt tomorrow, Samuel.
Take soldiers with you.

375
00:46:40,461 --> 00:46:42,561
I don't want any mistakes this time.

376
00:46:42,561 --> 00:46:45,141
Everything will proceed as we planned.

377
00:46:45,449 --> 00:46:48,569
There will be neither error
nor mishap, sir.

378
00:46:48,779 --> 00:46:51,129
Everything will be as you wanted.

379
00:46:59,759 --> 00:47:03,349
Do you realize how strong we are when
we are together, my dear friend?

380
00:47:03,427 --> 00:47:05,397
Of course.

381
00:47:05,601 --> 00:47:08,271
No one can stand against such a power.

382
00:47:10,093 --> 00:47:13,383
I want to strengthen this union
even more, Kosses.

383
00:47:15,152 --> 00:47:19,792
Alliances, ranks and even friendships
are doomed to fall.

384
00:47:21,234 --> 00:47:23,094
They are.

385
00:47:24,793 --> 00:47:26,143
But...

386
00:47:26,984 --> 00:47:28,954
But family.

387
00:47:29,663 --> 00:47:31,613
Is it like that?

388
00:47:38,311 --> 00:47:39,971
Family?

389
00:47:42,636 --> 00:47:44,466
Family means...

390
00:47:44,592 --> 00:47:48,252
being together for forever, Kosses.

391
00:47:52,076 --> 00:47:54,526
I don't like beating around the bush.

392
00:47:55,705 --> 00:47:58,055
I want to marry Mari.

393
00:48:01,837 --> 00:48:03,607
Is that so?

394
00:48:07,654 --> 00:48:09,454
There is no problem for me.

395
00:48:14,914 --> 00:48:17,984
But what Mari thinks about this?

396
00:48:18,512 --> 00:48:20,122
I will talk to her.

397
00:48:34,208 --> 00:48:36,818
The children are in Aya Yorgi Monastery.

398
00:48:37,881 --> 00:48:41,231
Then what are we waiting for my Bey?
Let's go and take our children.

399
00:48:41,515 --> 00:48:45,025
We need to take precautions, Demirci.

400
00:48:45,490 --> 00:48:47,750
Our enemies don't care about anything.

401
00:48:47,906 --> 00:48:51,686
We need to be careful so that nothing
happens to the children.

402
00:48:52,743 --> 00:48:54,323
What will we do, my Bey?

403
00:48:55,960 --> 00:48:58,350
We will send a spy to the monastery.

404
00:49:00,283 --> 00:49:02,443
I can go, my Bey.

405
00:49:02,796 --> 00:49:06,176
They will realize who you are
from your weapon.

406
00:49:06,221 --> 00:49:08,061
From your voice.

407
00:49:09,270 --> 00:49:11,720
A priest is coming from Constantinople.

408
00:49:13,467 --> 00:49:17,417
Someone should go to the
monastery instead of him.

409
00:49:18,897 --> 00:49:20,957
How can we make it possible, my Bey?

410
00:49:21,345 --> 00:49:25,035
Everyone in this camp has similar
features.

411
00:49:27,115 --> 00:49:29,935
Moreover, whoever will go
needs to pretend as a priest.

412
00:49:29,988 --> 00:49:31,698
You are right.

413
00:49:32,219 --> 00:49:34,949
That's why it needs to be someone that...

414
00:49:35,884 --> 00:49:37,874
doesn't arouse suspicion.

415
00:49:38,387 --> 00:49:40,127
Who can it be, my Bey?

416
00:49:40,436 --> 00:49:42,226
It is obvious who will do it.

417
00:49:43,442 --> 00:49:45,492
He will be here soon.

418
00:49:48,930 --> 00:49:51,020
Can I come in, Osman Bey?

419
00:49:51,277 --> 00:49:52,757
Come.

420
00:49:59,013 --> 00:50:00,893
You called me, my Bey.

421
00:50:03,123 --> 00:50:05,413
Is this the best you can find, my Bey?

422
00:50:16,247 --> 00:50:18,767
Brother, are you sure?

423
00:50:22,063 --> 00:50:24,503
I have a duty for you.

424
00:50:42,085 --> 00:50:43,725
Oh my.

425
00:50:53,746 --> 00:50:55,796
Oh my, Osman Bey.

426
00:51:03,316 --> 00:51:05,736
They are keeping our children in the
monastery.

427
00:51:08,243 --> 00:51:09,973
For our children...

428
00:51:10,613 --> 00:51:12,583
you need to wear this.

429
00:51:24,901 --> 00:51:29,681
There is no role we can't play to
save our children, my Bey.

430
00:51:55,979 --> 00:51:58,879
Aya Yorgi Monastery

431
00:52:04,224 --> 00:52:06,174
Alexander.

432
00:52:06,244 --> 00:52:08,514
This name suits you well.

433
00:52:10,704 --> 00:52:14,054
Future warriors of Jesus Christ.

434
00:52:15,061 --> 00:52:18,061
The monastery has been very good for you.

435
00:52:22,972 --> 00:52:24,682
What is this?

436
00:52:33,635 --> 00:52:37,919
You will not wear anything but the holy
cross...

437
00:52:37,919 --> 00:52:39,739
will you, Alexander?

438
00:52:40,041 --> 00:52:41,443
Get rid of this.

439
00:52:41,443 --> 00:52:44,553
Let me help you.

440
00:52:49,404 --> 00:52:51,504
You have no power to take this from me!

441
00:52:53,227 --> 00:52:54,787
What did you do?! Brother!

442
00:52:56,195 --> 00:52:58,090
What did you do?!

443
00:52:58,090 --> 00:53:00,990
Take them out of my sight!

444
00:53:01,221 --> 00:53:03,601
What did you do to him, huh?!

445
00:53:15,705 --> 00:53:18,925
I don't know where these Turks'
stubbornness comes from.

446
00:53:19,179 --> 00:53:23,439
But when they become good Christians
they will be of great use to me.

447
00:53:24,395 --> 00:53:27,915
But first, they will learn not to resist.

448
00:53:28,272 --> 00:53:30,272
I will discipline them all.

449
00:53:41,492 --> 00:53:43,672
In the name of Allah.

450
00:54:50,143 --> 00:54:51,933
My Allah.

451
00:54:53,168 --> 00:54:55,548
The hearts are in your hands.

452
00:54:59,812 --> 00:55:01,902
You know my faith and intention.

453
00:55:03,966 --> 00:55:06,536
You are the forgiver.

454
00:55:11,156 --> 00:55:13,866
Grant us to take our children from...

455
00:55:13,886 --> 00:55:16,256
the hands of our enemies with your help.

456
00:56:09,083 --> 00:56:12,773
Only fools carry the staff.

457
00:56:13,635 --> 00:56:16,235
I am entrusting it to you until
I fulfill my duty.

458
00:56:30,811 --> 00:56:33,721
I got it, Kumral Abdal.

459
00:57:20,916 --> 00:57:25,046
Unfortunately, your fun years in the
emperor's city...

460
00:57:25,611 --> 00:57:28,081
Constantinople are a thing of
the past, Mari.

461
00:57:28,431 --> 00:57:30,711
Our lands are in danger.

462
00:57:32,176 --> 00:57:35,446
We have to create a safe
and impassable line.

463
00:57:36,891 --> 00:57:39,851
And unfortunately, we can't
achieve that with an alliance.

464
00:57:40,899 --> 00:57:42,919
We need to be a family.

465
00:57:44,186 --> 00:57:48,026
You know well that kindredship comes first.

466
00:57:49,720 --> 00:57:51,910
What do you want to tell, brother?

467
00:57:55,552 --> 00:57:56,872
Nicola.

468
00:58:01,312 --> 00:58:03,402
He wants to marry you.

469
00:58:06,866 --> 00:58:10,606
Yes, I was nice to him a few
times for our purposes.

470
00:58:10,790 --> 00:58:13,760
But how can he find this
courage in himself?

471
00:58:16,839 --> 00:58:19,829
He went beyond the limits. I hope you put
himself in his place.

472
00:58:20,170 --> 00:58:22,560
It is you who is going beyond
the limits, Mari.

473
00:58:25,130 --> 00:58:27,758
I have already approved this marriage.

474
00:58:27,758 --> 00:58:31,127
You better prepare yourself as
soon as possible.

475
00:58:31,127 --> 00:58:32,537
No.

476
00:58:33,937 --> 00:58:36,357
I will never marry someone I don't want.

477
00:58:36,493 --> 00:58:40,543
I can't waste my life because of your
political ambitions, brother!

478
00:58:40,812 --> 00:58:43,616
Behave yourself, Mari. You are
going too far!

479
00:58:43,616 --> 00:58:45,746
I am your brother.

480
00:58:45,941 --> 00:58:50,021
You have lived freely until now, from now
on you will live for your family!

481
00:58:50,157 --> 00:58:51,201
Never!

482
00:58:51,201 --> 00:58:54,041
-You will marry!
-Never!

483
00:58:54,993 --> 00:58:57,613
You will never make me do
something I don't want.

484
00:59:27,976 --> 00:59:30,346
Can I come in, Malhun Hatun?

485
00:59:32,033 --> 00:59:34,143
Come, Bahadır.

486
00:59:46,777 --> 00:59:48,647
You can leave, Gökçe.

487
01:00:03,807 --> 01:00:06,047
What did you hear or see? What is
Gökçe doing?

488
01:00:06,197 --> 01:00:08,667
Apparently, she is hiding
something, Malhun Hatun.

489
01:00:09,912 --> 01:00:11,764
Sometimes she is dissappearing.

490
01:00:11,764 --> 01:00:13,457
I don't know where she is going.

491
01:00:13,457 --> 01:00:15,237
You will know, Bahadır.

492
01:00:16,402 --> 01:00:18,442
You will watch her closely.

493
01:00:18,505 --> 01:00:22,185
You will know where she is going, who she
meets with and what she is doing.

494
01:00:30,570 --> 01:00:34,030
I had this edict prepared for you so that
Rogatus will not suspect you.

495
01:00:37,154 --> 01:00:39,394
It will be your key for entering
the monastery.

496
01:00:42,395 --> 01:00:44,125
May Allah be with you.

497
01:00:44,720 --> 01:00:47,900
Kumral Abdal, bring our children
to us as soon as possible.

498
01:00:48,216 --> 01:00:50,316
We will be waiting for you here.

499
01:00:50,910 --> 01:00:52,370
Go safely.

500
01:00:52,370 --> 01:00:56,130
Don't worry. You gave the duty to most
appropriate man, my Bey.

501
01:01:16,248 --> 01:01:19,848
My Bey, the real priest is coming.

502
01:01:21,375 --> 01:01:23,575
Kumral Abdal is their guest.

503
01:01:23,839 --> 01:01:26,209
And the real priest will be our guest.

504
01:01:29,359 --> 01:01:31,069
Let's get on the horses.

505
01:01:47,660 --> 01:01:50,420
Malhun Hatun is getting
suspicious more and more.

506
01:01:56,041 --> 01:01:58,311
it was obvious that this would happen.

507
01:01:58,498 --> 01:02:00,179
What will I do now?

508
01:02:00,179 --> 01:02:02,959
Keep calm, Gökçe.

509
01:02:05,161 --> 01:02:07,611
Would I ever let anything happen to you?

510
01:02:08,044 --> 01:02:10,524
Go get your belongings, we will run away.

511
01:02:11,369 --> 01:02:12,936
Where will we go?

512
01:02:12,936 --> 01:02:15,906
Don't worry. I have prepared everything.

513
01:02:17,128 --> 01:02:19,348
We can't stay here anymore.

514
01:02:20,365 --> 01:02:24,265
If you don't want us to die, trust me.

515
01:02:24,427 --> 01:02:27,305
How will we do this? What if
they come after us?

516
01:02:27,305 --> 01:02:30,705
Let's get out of here first.
The rest is easy.

517
01:02:37,046 --> 01:02:39,111
Thank you, brother Bahadır.

518
01:02:39,111 --> 01:02:41,521
Come on. Go and get prepared.

519
01:02:42,129 --> 01:02:43,649
Hurry up.

520
01:04:01,234 --> 01:04:06,214
A priest can't enter this land
without permission.

521
01:04:08,394 --> 01:04:10,914
It's obvious that you haven't got
permission from us.

522
01:04:11,541 --> 01:04:15,641
Now, return to the place you came
from, to Constantinople.

523
01:04:16,933 --> 01:04:19,383
My soldiers will accompany
you for a while.

524
01:04:25,072 --> 01:04:27,842
Aya Yorgi Monastery

525
01:04:46,687 --> 01:04:49,147
You must be the Priest Philip.

526
01:04:57,009 --> 01:05:01,189
May the love of Almighty Jesus be
with you, Landlord Rogatus.

527
01:05:13,312 --> 01:05:16,062
We were waiting for your arrival eagerly.

528
01:05:24,044 --> 01:05:26,844
Why did the emperor send you alone?

529
01:05:28,663 --> 01:05:32,053
A clergyman needs no protection.

530
01:05:35,768 --> 01:05:38,138
What protect us is the prayers.

531
01:05:44,128 --> 01:05:46,918
Which church have you been to before?

532
01:05:48,596 --> 01:05:50,756
Church of St. Mary...

533
01:05:50,982 --> 01:05:53,682
of Constantinople.

534
01:05:56,523 --> 01:05:59,463
I will serve the Almighty Jesus Christ
here from now on.

535
01:06:00,318 --> 01:06:02,078
Welcome.

536
01:06:02,175 --> 01:06:05,515
Your experience seems to make
our job much easier.

537
01:06:06,500 --> 01:06:08,870
The children that have come
are a bit rebellious.

538
01:06:13,666 --> 01:06:17,936
It's the same as what Jesus Christ
saw walking around in the synagogues.

539
01:06:19,923 --> 01:06:24,493
They must be confused and desolate
like herds without a shepherd.

540
01:06:25,895 --> 01:06:29,025
Matthew, chapter 9, verse 36.

541
01:06:30,419 --> 01:06:34,789
I have heard of your devotion to the
words of Jesus Christ, Landlord Rogatus.

542
01:06:36,869 --> 01:06:38,599
It seems what I heard is true.

543
01:06:40,136 --> 01:06:43,466
If you'll excuse me, I want to
see the children now.

544
01:06:58,950 --> 01:07:00,950
Do what I do.

545
01:07:14,820 --> 01:07:16,635
Monk, show him.

546
01:07:16,635 --> 01:07:20,535
Let him make a cross until there are
no traces of his degenerate Turkishness.

547
01:07:22,749 --> 01:07:23,963
Kneel!

548
01:07:23,963 --> 01:07:26,423
We only kneel in the presence of Allah.

549
01:07:45,795 --> 01:07:49,105
Didn't our religion forbid cruelty
to children?

550
01:07:49,633 --> 01:07:51,333
Yes, his serene highness.

551
01:07:54,968 --> 01:07:57,618
Blessed ones are the merciful people.

552
01:07:57,846 --> 01:08:00,586
Because they will get mercy.

553
01:08:02,547 --> 01:08:04,667
You must be the Priest Philip.

554
01:08:08,486 --> 01:08:10,271
Yes.

555
01:08:10,271 --> 01:08:13,721
I will take care of the children of
Jesus Christ from now on.

556
01:08:28,635 --> 01:08:33,095
I would like to see how you deliver
the teachings of Jesus Christ.

557
01:08:36,910 --> 01:08:39,720
Oh, my beautiful children.

558
01:08:46,885 --> 01:08:50,295
You will be connected to the
Almighty Jesus Christ with love.

559
01:08:53,609 --> 01:08:58,649
In time, Christian teachings will meet
in your memory.

560
01:09:00,365 --> 01:09:02,694
What are you saying, Priest?!

561
01:09:04,252 --> 01:09:06,803
Go and tell this to your own children.

562
01:09:07,194 --> 01:09:08,834
Leave us alone.

563
01:09:09,566 --> 01:09:12,986
Don't test my anger,
little mouse. Be obedient!

564
01:09:23,236 --> 01:09:28,076
Every word is a pearl in our holy book.

565
01:09:29,517 --> 01:09:34,617
It says there; "Salvation comes
only with patience."

566
01:09:41,066 --> 01:09:45,666
Be happy with your hope
and endure adversities.

567
01:09:49,024 --> 01:09:51,665
Devote yourself to prayers.

568
01:09:57,739 --> 01:09:59,769
Let's not make our children exhausted.

569
01:09:59,926 --> 01:10:02,076
It's enough for today.

570
01:10:24,435 --> 01:10:28,145
My brothers, Osman Bey will save us.

571
01:10:46,019 --> 01:10:49,849
Let's go, Bahadir.
I don't want to spend one more second here.

572
01:10:50,341 --> 01:10:52,571
Let's go Gokce girl.

573
01:10:59,883 --> 01:11:01,863
We are free, right?

574
01:11:01,969 --> 01:11:03,729
We are, yes.

575
01:11:05,059 --> 01:11:07,429
Hide Gokce girl.

576
01:11:32,242 --> 01:11:33,702
Let's go.

577
01:11:36,153 --> 01:11:37,893
Bahadir?

578
01:11:43,071 --> 01:11:47,561
You need to die so that
I can live, Gokce.

579
01:13:08,677 --> 01:13:13,657
So, our Monastery's fame is
all over Constantinople.

580
01:13:14,426 --> 01:13:16,016
Yes.

581
01:13:16,144 --> 01:13:18,854
Emperor is pleased.

582
01:13:19,364 --> 01:13:24,314
If this goes on like that, we'll need another
Monastery in Bilecik, he says.

583
01:13:24,771 --> 01:13:28,116
Because we'll teach Christianity
to all the Turkish children.

584
01:13:29,866 --> 01:13:33,926
Do you really believe that those little
devils can settle down with love?

585
01:13:35,130 --> 01:13:38,390
Jesus Christ's love shall fill your heart,
sister Julia.

586
01:13:39,281 --> 01:13:42,881
Mercy is sharper than a sword.

587
01:13:43,194 --> 01:13:47,514
It is so sharp that it can make one
love his enemy.

588
01:13:48,582 --> 01:13:52,842
These children will love us
through our mercy.

589
01:13:56,731 --> 01:14:00,701
By the way, I want you to manage the ritual
in the church in Bilecik...

590
01:14:00,721 --> 01:14:02,711
...at Feast of the Annunciation.

591
01:14:02,711 --> 01:14:05,591
Also, you'd recite verses from
John the Apostle.

592
01:14:06,088 --> 01:14:09,918
I'd love to! Little time left to
Feast of the Annunciation.

593
01:14:23,824 --> 01:14:26,274
But, Lord Rogatus...

594
01:14:26,869 --> 01:14:30,359
I can recite verses from
John the Apostle later.

595
01:14:31,452 --> 01:14:34,012
Because Gospel of Luke is recited
in Feast of the Annunciation.

596
01:14:42,527 --> 01:14:45,397
God's lamb shall be with you.

597
01:14:57,319 --> 01:14:59,179
Brothers...

598
01:14:59,247 --> 01:15:01,437
...we'll get out of here...

599
01:15:01,553 --> 01:15:04,833
...just like how Kumral Abdal said.

600
01:15:29,821 --> 01:15:31,941
For Jesus Christ!

601
01:15:33,008 --> 01:15:36,328
You are on foot all day for
these children...

602
01:15:36,328 --> 01:15:38,978
who are the future of Christianity!

603
01:15:39,245 --> 01:15:41,865
Without us, they would run away, father.

604
01:15:46,426 --> 01:15:50,476
You are Jesus Christ's loyal servants.

605
01:15:56,945 --> 01:15:59,245
But you are sinners.

606
01:15:59,870 --> 01:16:04,230
So many!
I see the hell!

607
01:16:15,615 --> 01:16:18,055
Don't you visit the church?

608
01:16:18,962 --> 01:16:23,092
Father, we spend all our time
waiting here.

609
01:16:23,713 --> 01:16:26,033
We can't even attend rituals
here.

610
01:16:27,263 --> 01:16:29,163
Something must be done.

611
01:16:29,359 --> 01:16:32,599
I can't watch you go to
hell like this.

612
01:16:37,354 --> 01:16:39,634
I will bless you right here.

613
01:16:39,643 --> 01:16:42,023
You'll be cleansed from
your sins.

614
01:16:44,834 --> 01:16:46,604
Come here.

615
01:16:47,833 --> 01:16:49,213
You too, my child.

616
01:16:51,614 --> 01:16:53,234
Come.

617
01:16:55,991 --> 01:16:57,751
Sit.

618
01:17:02,570 --> 01:17:05,260
Close your eyes.

619
01:17:07,123 --> 01:17:10,643
It will be like you are
baptized again.

620
01:17:31,997 --> 01:17:36,907
You need to be tied to
each other first.

621
01:17:39,376 --> 01:17:42,846
He is more knowledgeable than
any priest I know.

622
01:17:43,685 --> 01:17:45,885
He influences you.

623
01:17:49,678 --> 01:17:53,248
You are the loyal servants
of Jesus Christ.

624
01:17:53,313 --> 01:17:58,213
Stay close, so that evil
can't pass through your friendship.

625
01:18:02,571 --> 01:18:07,351
My God, our father and
your son Jesus Christ...

626
01:18:10,168 --> 01:18:14,298
protect us from our friends' betrayals!

627
01:18:36,531 --> 01:18:38,381
Breath.

628
01:18:39,047 --> 01:18:40,747
Breath.

629
01:18:45,684 --> 01:18:47,624
Breath.

630
01:18:58,760 --> 01:19:01,080
Kayı's warriors!

631
01:19:01,700 --> 01:19:03,820
May Allah bless you!

632
01:19:05,139 --> 01:19:07,859
Thank Allah!
Mashallah!

633
01:19:08,106 --> 01:19:11,016
Thank Allah!
Come on!

634
01:19:11,543 --> 01:19:14,103
Osman Bey is waiting.

635
01:19:17,494 --> 01:19:19,184
But...

636
01:19:22,163 --> 01:19:25,353
why did he say 'God's sheep'?

637
01:19:28,171 --> 01:19:30,621
He should've said Agnus Dei.

638
01:19:32,068 --> 01:19:34,168
Why didn't he say it in Latin?

639
01:19:37,478 --> 01:19:40,338
Priests say it in Latin.

640
01:19:41,112 --> 01:19:44,982
And this priest is coming from
Constantinople.

641
01:19:49,306 --> 01:19:52,536
Do you think that the priest
doesn't know Latin?

642
01:19:54,215 --> 01:19:58,585
A priest with such knowledge
must know Latin.

643
01:19:59,327 --> 01:20:00,817
Right?

644
01:20:13,257 --> 01:20:15,997
Come on.
Come on.

645
01:20:30,042 --> 01:20:34,262
Where are you going, Priest Philip?

646
01:20:53,109 --> 01:20:58,049
To feed my children, Lord Rogatus.

647
01:21:02,464 --> 01:21:05,934
You shouldn't have bothered.

648
01:21:06,498 --> 01:21:10,178
Education starts in the kitchen.

649
01:21:10,379 --> 01:21:12,879
This is a pleasure for me.

650
01:21:17,887 --> 01:21:21,027
I'm glad we have you, father.

651
01:21:25,514 --> 01:21:27,774
Please, go on.

652
01:22:16,203 --> 01:22:17,963
Soldiers?

653
01:22:27,042 --> 01:22:28,722
Father?

654
01:22:29,263 --> 01:22:32,143
Damn it! Soldiers!

655
01:22:32,518 --> 01:22:36,848
Soldiers! Stop the priest!
Stop the priest!

656
01:22:48,226 --> 01:22:50,346
Come on, Kumral Abdal.

657
01:22:52,894 --> 01:22:54,674
Bring our valiants back.

658
01:23:05,591 --> 01:23:10,021
My bey, inshallah Kumral Abdal
succeeds.

659
01:23:10,820 --> 01:23:15,380
Göktuğ! Who do you think
Kumral Abdal is?

660
01:23:17,382 --> 01:23:20,552
He was back to back with
Sarı Saltuk in many battles.

661
01:23:21,377 --> 01:23:23,667
He disguises so well that...

662
01:23:23,819 --> 01:23:26,399
even the heathens see him as
one of them.

663
01:23:27,221 --> 01:23:29,001
Alright, my bey.

664
01:23:32,955 --> 01:23:35,295
We'll get our children.

665
01:23:36,278 --> 01:23:38,858
We won't leave them to the heathens!

666
01:23:52,309 --> 01:23:54,209
Stop! Don't run!

667
01:23:55,960 --> 01:23:57,640
Children.

668
01:23:58,745 --> 01:24:01,185
Alps! Come on!

669
01:24:02,577 --> 01:24:04,307
Come on!

670
01:24:14,106 --> 01:24:15,916
Stop!

671
01:24:31,343 --> 01:24:33,333
Alps!

672
01:24:33,635 --> 01:24:35,645
Charge!

673
01:24:38,447 --> 01:24:40,607
Osman Bey!
Osman Bey!

674
01:24:47,066 --> 01:24:48,796
Osman!

675
01:24:59,218 --> 01:25:01,418
-Come on!
-Osman Bey!

676
01:25:01,814 --> 01:25:03,394
Hurry!

677
01:25:05,140 --> 01:25:07,370
Hurry! Run!

678
01:25:09,020 --> 01:25:11,220
Hurry!

679
01:25:28,242 --> 01:25:30,287
My valiants!
Are you alright?

680
01:25:30,287 --> 01:25:34,107
We didn't bow, my bey.
We showed them the Kayı!

681
01:25:34,373 --> 01:25:37,063
Mashallah to my valiants!

682
01:25:38,832 --> 01:25:40,622
My lions!

683
01:25:41,858 --> 01:25:43,468
My lions!

684
01:25:44,967 --> 01:25:46,901
Come on! Come on!

685
01:25:46,901 --> 01:25:48,631
Come on!

686
01:26:05,576 --> 01:26:07,292
Give me the relic.

687
01:26:07,292 --> 01:26:08,912
Oh, Kumral Abdal.

688
01:26:11,708 --> 01:26:13,398
We are retreating!

689
01:26:18,742 --> 01:26:20,972
I will kill you all!

690
01:26:24,121 --> 01:26:26,321
Boran!

691
01:26:42,885 --> 01:26:44,359
Are you alright, Kumral Abdal?

692
01:26:44,359 --> 01:26:46,149
Thank Allah, my bey.

693
01:26:46,246 --> 01:26:47,776
Mashallah!

694
01:26:48,042 --> 01:26:49,132
Come on!

695
01:26:49,585 --> 01:26:51,465
Boran, come on!

696
01:26:53,889 --> 01:26:55,759
Boran!

697
01:26:55,784 --> 01:26:58,044
I also feel the fire of Gonca
in me!

698
01:26:58,325 --> 01:27:00,624
But we'll go for the children!

699
01:27:00,624 --> 01:27:02,094
My bey.

700
01:27:02,424 --> 01:27:05,244
Boran! Come on!

701
01:27:07,232 --> 01:27:08,624
Alps!

702
01:27:08,624 --> 01:27:10,854
I won't die before you, weasel!

703
01:27:11,432 --> 01:27:13,294
I will come back for you!

704
01:27:13,294 --> 01:27:15,814
I will return for you!

705
01:27:38,819 --> 01:27:40,759
Let them go!

706
01:27:41,021 --> 01:27:42,471
Let them!

707
01:27:46,504 --> 01:27:48,274
Idiots!

708
01:27:50,161 --> 01:27:52,141
Army of idiots!

709
01:27:53,168 --> 01:27:56,238
You couldn't take care of a handful
of kids!

710
01:27:56,509 --> 01:28:00,469
A handful of kids!
Why are you dying?

711
01:28:00,472 --> 01:28:03,102
Why are you dying?
Idiots!

712
01:28:03,614 --> 01:28:06,574
We couldn't take care of
a handful of kids!

713
01:28:11,104 --> 01:28:13,814
Turgut Bey's Tribe

714
01:28:20,451 --> 01:28:22,411
Are you out of strenght?

715
01:28:23,208 --> 01:28:25,588
Are your knees weak?

716
01:28:25,977 --> 01:28:30,187
Don't forget!
Your sword is a part of you.

717
01:28:30,608 --> 01:28:32,348
You won't let it fall!

718
01:28:43,915 --> 01:28:46,455
Come on. Take it.

719
01:29:03,877 --> 01:29:07,267
You are sweaty!

720
01:29:07,843 --> 01:29:11,473
But it's good. Those who sweat
the most in the training...

721
01:29:11,803 --> 01:29:14,143
bleeds the least on the battlefield!

722
01:29:16,750 --> 01:29:18,370
Come on.

723
01:29:19,499 --> 01:29:21,289
It's enough for now.

724
01:29:24,714 --> 01:29:26,634
Everyone to your jobs!

725
01:29:26,948 --> 01:29:28,878
Remember what I said, alps!

726
01:29:37,350 --> 01:29:38,940
Mari.

727
01:29:39,825 --> 01:29:42,515
Won't you welcome me?

728
01:29:43,114 --> 01:29:44,994
I'm surprised.

729
01:29:45,147 --> 01:29:47,037
But of course, welcome.

730
01:29:48,313 --> 01:29:51,323
I want to talk to you about something,
Turgut Bey.

731
01:29:51,943 --> 01:29:53,473
Go on.

732
01:29:53,790 --> 01:29:55,310
I'm listening.

733
01:29:55,980 --> 01:30:00,180
If you are here for breaking the
agreement, it's long done.

734
01:30:03,807 --> 01:30:06,687
Won't you invite me inside?

735
01:30:09,503 --> 01:30:11,383
Sorry about that.

736
01:30:12,068 --> 01:30:14,698
Come, let's get into the tent.

737
01:30:31,052 --> 01:30:33,772
Hay Masha Allah(praise be) my Orhan.

738
01:30:36,191 --> 01:30:38,411
Attaboy of his mother!

739
01:30:39,957 --> 01:30:41,357
Can I come in?

740
01:30:44,080 --> 01:30:46,010
Come Bahadır.

741
01:30:55,461 --> 01:30:58,061
Bahadır?
What happened?

742
01:30:58,548 --> 01:30:59,778
What happened to you?

743
01:31:01,628 --> 01:31:04,508
I saw Gokce leaving the tent secretly.

744
01:31:04,698 --> 01:31:06,928
- So?
- I followed her.

745
01:31:07,535 --> 01:31:10,375
She met the soldiers of Lord in forest.

746
01:31:12,677 --> 01:31:14,437
They talked a little.

747
01:31:14,641 --> 01:31:16,881
The man gave her a pocket.

748
01:31:21,091 --> 01:31:24,231
The soldier realized me at that time.

749
01:31:25,042 --> 01:31:26,652
We fought.

750
01:31:27,730 --> 01:31:30,620
I got Gokce, I wanted to take her to you.

751
01:31:31,693 --> 01:31:34,283
She and the soldier united against me.

752
01:31:36,606 --> 01:31:38,556
She run away with him..

753
01:31:38,601 --> 01:31:40,921
- Malhun Hatun.
- Traitor!

754
01:31:47,757 --> 01:31:49,217
Forgive me, my Hanim(lady).

755
01:31:49,558 --> 01:31:51,408
I should have realised it earlier.

756
01:31:53,428 --> 01:31:55,878
Gokce tricked us all.

757
01:31:57,774 --> 01:32:01,364
However, you should have realised.

758
01:32:07,609 --> 01:32:09,379
You are still bleeding.

759
01:32:09,927 --> 01:32:12,067
Have your wound checked.

760
01:32:22,686 --> 01:32:24,266
Gokce!

761
01:32:27,301 --> 01:32:29,301
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim
(In the name of Allah, the merciful, the compassionate).

762
01:32:47,691 --> 01:32:49,971
You are not used to this,
Byzantine Beauty.

763
01:32:51,669 --> 01:32:53,759
It's not like your dinner table.

764
01:32:54,290 --> 01:32:56,500
Yes, you Turks are different.

765
01:32:58,973 --> 01:33:00,553
So tell me.

766
01:33:01,202 --> 01:33:04,292
What brought you here?

767
01:33:08,202 --> 01:33:10,074
I wondered about you.

768
01:33:10,467 --> 01:33:12,287
How has your arm been?

769
01:33:16,396 --> 01:33:18,386
You know what happened at the castle.

770
01:33:19,538 --> 01:33:20,988
And that the trade is over.

771
01:33:23,518 --> 01:33:25,518
We are not friends anymore.

772
01:33:26,550 --> 01:33:27,990
Why did you wonder?

773
01:33:28,345 --> 01:33:30,655
Yes, I know it all, Turgut Bey.

774
01:33:31,601 --> 01:33:35,451
What happens between you and my brother
doesn't interest me.

775
01:33:37,496 --> 01:33:40,296
Also, there is a good cause
for all of this.

776
01:33:40,614 --> 01:33:42,334
I agree...

777
01:33:42,507 --> 01:33:44,877
Involving children is cruel.

778
01:33:47,150 --> 01:33:50,520
That being said, infiltrating into the
castle to save the children...

779
01:33:51,445 --> 01:33:53,495
is very brave.

780
01:33:53,620 --> 01:33:56,690
No matter what is it about, Mari, ...

781
01:33:56,892 --> 01:34:00,242
... I won't let anyone find peace if they
touche children.

782
01:34:01,912 --> 01:34:04,072
Speaking of which, do you have a child?

783
01:34:06,510 --> 01:34:09,000
Turks marry early as far as I know.

784
01:34:10,338 --> 01:34:12,028
Haven't you married yet?

785
01:34:21,687 --> 01:34:23,187
I was married.

786
01:34:25,931 --> 01:34:27,911
Destiny...

787
01:34:29,232 --> 01:34:32,122
My Hatun died...

788
01:34:33,692 --> 01:34:35,132
...untimely.

789
01:34:38,294 --> 01:34:39,774
Then I...

790
01:34:44,617 --> 01:34:46,707
I didn't know.
I am sorry.

791
01:34:51,468 --> 01:34:53,928
I was wondering about one more thing.

792
01:34:56,539 --> 01:35:00,429
In your traditions, is a woman forced
to marry someone she doesn't want?

793
01:35:00,455 --> 01:35:02,035
Never.

794
01:35:02,747 --> 01:35:07,327
We first ask the woman if she wants him.

795
01:35:08,478 --> 01:35:10,658
We don't force our Hatuns.

796
01:35:13,215 --> 01:35:15,375
Why are you asking these?

797
01:35:16,761 --> 01:35:18,241
I wondered.

798
01:35:24,325 --> 01:35:25,795
To be honest...

799
01:35:27,402 --> 01:35:30,402
My brother wants to marry me off to Nicola
without my will.

800
01:35:41,509 --> 01:35:43,759
Why are you telling me this, Mari?

801
01:35:51,177 --> 01:35:53,177
I should leave.

802
01:35:53,315 --> 01:35:55,175
Thanks for dinner.

803
01:36:02,291 --> 01:36:03,841
Can I come in, my Bey?

804
01:36:11,898 --> 01:36:14,118
What are they asking for again, my Bey?

805
01:36:14,603 --> 01:36:16,863
Mari's helper hasn't said a word either.

806
01:36:20,842 --> 01:36:22,162
My Bey?

807
01:36:22,787 --> 01:36:24,447
I don't know, Kutan.

808
01:36:25,103 --> 01:36:26,713
I don't know.

809
01:36:29,476 --> 01:36:31,626
She doesn't know what she wants.

810
01:36:33,406 --> 01:36:35,276
And I don't either.

811
01:37:22,289 --> 01:37:23,789
Argos!

812
01:37:25,559 --> 01:37:29,549
It is time to hit the deathblow, Argos!

813
01:37:32,073 --> 01:37:35,206
My soldiers... are my soldiers ready?

814
01:37:35,206 --> 01:37:36,826
They are, sir!

815
01:37:44,558 --> 01:37:47,208
I like vandalizing!

816
01:37:52,339 --> 01:37:53,749
Osman!

817
01:37:54,491 --> 01:37:56,851
Osman took the children, Nicola!

818
01:37:56,851 --> 01:37:59,321
This is not important anymore,
my saint friend.

819
01:37:59,321 --> 01:38:01,270
We'll burn Sogut down.

820
01:38:01,863 --> 01:38:04,908
Those Greek Fires are everywhere in
mosques, khanqahs...

821
01:38:04,908 --> 01:38:08,398
...bazaars, everywhere!
We'll burn Sogut down!

822
01:38:09,427 --> 01:38:11,617
I want to take revenge on
Osman immediately!

823
01:38:11,638 --> 01:38:13,238
We shall burn them down!

824
01:38:13,323 --> 01:38:15,083
Let's not make Kosses wait.

825
01:39:08,330 --> 01:39:09,580
Ahmet!

826
01:39:09,630 --> 01:39:11,130
Mother!

827
01:39:11,891 --> 01:39:13,801
- Ahmet!
- Mother Bala!

828
01:39:13,990 --> 01:39:15,850
Ahmet! Ahmet!

829
01:39:18,350 --> 01:39:19,548
Mother Bala!

830
01:39:19,670 --> 01:39:20,720
My Ahmet.

831
01:39:22,371 --> 01:39:23,621
My Ahmet.

832
01:39:29,595 --> 01:39:32,295
Thank Allah!
Welcome!

833
01:39:45,947 --> 01:39:47,347
My Ahmet.

834
01:39:49,613 --> 01:39:51,153
My Ahmet.

835
01:39:55,348 --> 01:39:57,298
- My Osman!
- Mother!

836
01:39:58,053 --> 01:39:59,493
Mother.

837
01:40:00,283 --> 01:40:02,983
- Welcome son.
- Thank you.

838
01:40:04,228 --> 01:40:05,958
May Allah bless you my Bey!

839
01:40:06,474 --> 01:40:08,704
- Bala.
- Osman.

840
01:40:11,320 --> 01:40:13,322
Long live Osman Bey!

841
01:40:14,361 --> 01:40:16,991
We found them thanks to my valiant!

842
01:40:20,317 --> 01:40:22,427
Hay Masha Allah my lion!

843
01:40:25,203 --> 01:40:28,093
You brought their sons to mothers.

844
01:40:28,365 --> 01:40:30,455
You dashed their tears away.

845
01:40:37,839 --> 01:40:41,209
Now you shall hug your child.

846
01:40:46,541 --> 01:40:48,331
My Orhan.

847
01:40:51,828 --> 01:40:53,358
My Orhan.

848
01:40:54,129 --> 01:40:55,639
Masha Allah (praise be).

849
01:41:14,872 --> 01:41:16,662
Masha Allah my lion.

850
01:41:32,376 --> 01:41:33,536
Infidels...

851
01:41:35,081 --> 01:41:37,041
...exceeded their limits...

852
01:41:38,368 --> 01:41:40,638
...intended to take our children away!

853
01:41:43,038 --> 01:41:44,448
...Mothers...

854
01:41:45,238 --> 01:41:46,478
...Fathers...

855
01:41:46,919 --> 01:41:49,229
...cried a lot.

856
01:41:50,157 --> 01:41:52,387
They hardened their heart!

857
01:41:54,150 --> 01:41:58,840
Their aim was to change our children's
religion.

858
01:42:01,602 --> 01:42:07,392
They wanted to vanish the love of
Allah and prophet.

859
01:42:10,491 --> 01:42:12,611
However, they don't know that...

860
01:42:12,947 --> 01:42:16,967
we have raised them with the names
of Allah and Quran...

861
01:42:17,181 --> 01:42:19,531
... since their childhood!

862
01:42:23,500 --> 01:42:27,640
They grew their faith inside!

863
01:42:28,829 --> 01:42:31,329
Like a mighty plane tree.

864
01:42:35,907 --> 01:42:38,137
A hard-rooted person...

865
01:42:38,582 --> 01:42:40,962
...doesn't give up on their belief easily!

866
01:42:41,435 --> 01:42:43,465
Not even by force of a sword!

867
01:42:45,629 --> 01:42:48,319
Thanks to holy Allah first...

868
01:42:49,731 --> 01:42:52,271
Then thanks to the wisdom of our children...

869
01:42:53,470 --> 01:42:55,480
We overcame this trouble.

870
01:42:57,560 --> 01:42:59,970
May my Allah bless my valiants!

871
01:43:00,328 --> 01:43:03,038
Amin!

872
01:43:05,207 --> 01:43:09,617
You don't mention yourself Osman Bey!
Our children are here thanks to you!

873
01:43:09,701 --> 01:43:12,601
May Allah bless you my Bey!

874
01:43:17,632 --> 01:43:19,742
It's beyond myself.

875
01:43:20,636 --> 01:43:22,426
It's beyond Beyship.

876
01:43:22,836 --> 01:43:24,816
It's beyond my life.

877
01:43:25,784 --> 01:43:30,574
My life is in service of the Dawah!

878
01:43:32,119 --> 01:43:34,667
Our road shall end in Kizilelma!

879
01:43:38,577 --> 01:43:56,137
Allah-u Akbar!
(Allah is the greatest!)

880
01:43:57,307 --> 01:43:59,197
Sogut.

881
01:44:50,729 --> 01:44:52,571
Your words are lovely.

882
01:44:52,571 --> 01:44:57,021
But this love is not in your holy book,
Sheik Edeali.

883
01:44:59,732 --> 01:45:04,002
Your book says God loves only Muslims.

884
01:45:05,126 --> 01:45:09,656
Do you know how we start doing
something, Gregor?

885
01:45:12,301 --> 01:45:16,701
We start in the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

886
01:45:18,534 --> 01:45:20,714
Do you know what
rahman(merciful) means?

887
01:45:22,045 --> 01:45:24,475
No, I don't.

888
01:45:24,679 --> 01:45:29,879
Rahman is one of the finest
names of our holy creator.

889
01:45:32,140 --> 01:45:38,070
That name describes his mercifulness
for all of the people.

890
01:45:41,262 --> 01:45:43,722
That breath you take, Gregor...

891
01:45:44,683 --> 01:45:46,753
...that eyes of yours...

892
01:45:48,720 --> 01:45:54,780
...All of them are the reflection of
the name Rahman.

893
01:45:57,727 --> 01:46:02,007
He gaves His blessings to everyone.

894
01:46:02,509 --> 01:46:05,209
He doesn't differentiate.

895
01:46:08,147 --> 01:46:09,557
But...

896
01:46:10,387 --> 01:46:12,857
If one's heart is dark...

897
01:46:13,086 --> 01:46:16,836
They ignore His blessings.

898
01:46:18,137 --> 01:46:22,687
Your words are influencing,
my friend Edebalı.

899
01:46:24,052 --> 01:46:26,702
Estagfirullah.
(Thanks).

900
01:46:27,853 --> 01:46:32,193
If my words were influencing...

901
01:46:32,911 --> 01:46:37,621
Sogut would be blooming.

902
01:46:45,586 --> 01:46:49,276
My words doesn't come from me...

903
01:46:50,792 --> 01:46:52,632
They come from the Rahman (merciful Allah).

904
01:47:08,819 --> 01:47:12,509
We shall not take your precious time
any longer, my friend Edebali.

905
01:47:20,136 --> 01:47:25,366
The doors of our heart and the doors
of our khanqah are always open to you.

906
01:49:33,149 --> 01:49:34,219
My Bey!

907
01:49:34,333 --> 01:49:37,293
They tried to deceive us by inviting us
to the dinner table!

908
01:49:39,045 --> 01:49:41,495
But none of us ate!

909
01:49:42,608 --> 01:49:44,748
We said we don't eat pork.

910
01:49:45,437 --> 01:49:47,957
Masha Allah. Masha Allah!

911
01:49:48,925 --> 01:49:53,215
The most beautiful halal prizes are
for the ones who don't touch haram, Ahmet.

912
01:50:17,343 --> 01:50:19,273
So, my valiants.

913
01:50:22,595 --> 01:50:24,345
Here we go.

914
01:50:26,065 --> 01:50:29,035
I slaughtered a lamb for
the valiants of tent.

915
01:50:29,048 --> 01:50:31,838
In the names of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

916
01:50:31,870 --> 01:50:36,730
Touching the banned is haram while
such food are available for you.

917
01:50:38,046 --> 01:50:41,336
So, enjoy your meal!

918
01:50:46,085 --> 01:50:47,735
Take it, my valiant.

919
01:51:02,628 --> 01:51:04,298
Here we go.

920
01:51:20,530 --> 01:51:22,640
How could you bear hunger...

921
01:51:23,510 --> 01:51:25,860
...with your little body?

922
01:51:25,905 --> 01:51:28,085
We bear with the power of faith.

923
01:51:29,291 --> 01:51:33,001
Kumral Abdal told us about Hadrat Ali.

924
01:51:34,702 --> 01:51:37,332
We drew ourselves up against the infidels
like him.

925
01:51:40,773 --> 01:51:43,053
If I had a Zulfiqar (Ali's sword)...

926
01:51:43,477 --> 01:51:45,407
imagine what I would do!

927
01:51:46,900 --> 01:51:50,890
You didn't have a sword but you
stabbed the Lord with a fork!

928
01:51:52,439 --> 01:51:54,919
Masha Allah my valiants!

929
01:51:55,243 --> 01:51:57,113
Look at them!

930
01:51:57,696 --> 01:51:59,356
As long as we have valiants like you...

931
01:52:01,538 --> 01:52:03,688
...founding a state is close.

932
01:52:07,700 --> 01:52:09,560
Let's eat.

933
01:52:19,195 --> 01:52:21,090
Good luck with it, Davut Agha.

934
01:52:21,090 --> 01:52:23,410
Your swords shall be sharp!

935
01:52:28,294 --> 01:52:31,974
Who am I talking to?

936
01:52:32,766 --> 01:52:35,616
I am forging a cross for you!

937
01:52:36,932 --> 01:52:38,972
What are you talking about blacksmith?

938
01:52:39,563 --> 01:52:42,193
Wait until you see it!

939
01:52:46,124 --> 01:52:49,124
Ha! I told the tailor to prepare
a priest clothe for you.

940
01:52:55,142 --> 01:52:59,302
My Allah, accept Abdal's prayers.

941
01:52:59,660 --> 01:53:02,050
I am seeking for your help.

942
01:53:02,774 --> 01:53:04,564
Give me patience.

943
01:53:05,697 --> 01:53:09,087
My Kumral! You shall be patient.

944
01:53:09,708 --> 01:53:12,488
Tell me.
How did they not realise you?

945
01:53:12,631 --> 01:53:14,971
How did you save our children?

946
01:53:30,043 --> 01:53:32,563
I learned leaving no track behind...

947
01:53:32,642 --> 01:53:35,052
...from Saltug.

948
01:53:35,838 --> 01:53:37,238
They didn't realise.

949
01:53:37,346 --> 01:53:39,866
Masha Allah. Masha Allah.

950
01:53:40,112 --> 01:53:42,972
After all, you'd make a good priest.

951
01:53:44,523 --> 01:53:45,901
What did you say?

952
01:53:45,901 --> 01:53:49,283
Nothing, nothing.
You are a skillful imitator...

953
01:53:49,333 --> 01:53:52,263
...that's all I am saying.

954
01:53:53,504 --> 01:53:56,804
You are Saltug's student, that's why.

955
01:53:57,651 --> 01:54:00,761
My Kumral, may Allah bless you.

956
01:54:01,173 --> 01:54:04,643
Mothers hugged their children
thanks to you.

957
01:54:06,823 --> 01:54:10,053
Shut up!
I did nothing important.

958
01:54:10,208 --> 01:54:12,498
Don't talk like that again.

959
01:54:13,214 --> 01:54:16,104
Everything is done with the help of Allah.

960
01:54:24,049 --> 01:54:27,819
We have countless crazies in our tribe!

961
01:54:49,713 --> 01:54:51,403
Aygül Hatun.

962
01:54:54,268 --> 01:54:55,898
Cerkutay.

963
01:54:56,096 --> 01:54:57,906
Why do you not want me?

964
01:54:59,146 --> 01:55:00,836
Is it because I am ugly?

965
01:55:02,724 --> 01:55:04,184
No.

966
01:55:05,415 --> 01:55:07,645
Then it must be because I eat too much.

967
01:55:09,891 --> 01:55:11,341
No.

968
01:55:15,295 --> 01:55:17,015
Because I am crazy?

969
01:55:18,334 --> 01:55:20,434
I am crazier than you.

970
01:55:22,875 --> 01:55:24,175
Right.

971
01:55:25,184 --> 01:55:29,394
Then why don't you want me, crazy girl?

972
01:55:38,487 --> 01:55:40,167
Cerkutay.

973
01:55:42,133 --> 01:55:45,473
You are a good man.

974
01:55:48,692 --> 01:55:50,422
You are brave.

975
01:55:51,829 --> 01:55:53,819
You are merciful.

976
01:55:53,984 --> 01:55:55,634
You are manful.

977
01:55:55,784 --> 01:55:57,324
But..

978
01:55:58,121 --> 01:56:00,631
I am afraid to fall again.

979
01:56:02,731 --> 01:56:04,781
I am afraid, Cerkutay.

980
01:56:08,092 --> 01:56:10,102
Cerkutay won't fall!

981
01:56:12,683 --> 01:56:14,613
I stand still.

982
01:56:14,902 --> 01:56:16,642
I will not let you fall.

983
01:56:18,308 --> 01:56:21,608
I will stand behind your back!

984
01:56:21,608 --> 01:56:24,268
I won't fall even in an earthquake!

985
01:56:25,527 --> 01:56:26,597
Also...

986
01:56:27,696 --> 01:56:30,266
War is tougher than life.

987
01:56:32,154 --> 01:56:35,184
You leaned on Cerkutay at war.

988
01:56:35,656 --> 01:56:37,646
Why not now?

989
01:56:42,382 --> 01:56:45,312
You'll come to me crazy girl!

990
01:56:45,559 --> 01:56:46,769
Sshh!

991
01:56:56,897 --> 01:56:58,737
I'll wait.

992
01:57:00,980 --> 01:57:03,060
Cerkutay won't give up!

993
01:57:03,783 --> 01:57:04,853
Also...

994
01:57:13,792 --> 01:57:15,202
Also...

995
01:57:16,054 --> 01:57:18,324
Love cannot be given up.

996
01:57:23,007 --> 01:57:25,157
Sogut.

997
01:57:26,329 --> 01:57:29,059
We placed the Greek Fire where
we wanted.

998
01:57:29,538 --> 01:57:32,421
Sogut will burn down with our sign.

999
01:57:32,421 --> 01:57:33,951
Excellent.

1000
01:57:34,337 --> 01:57:37,747
Sogut will burn down in their sleep.

1001
01:57:37,895 --> 01:57:39,975
Do not have doubt Priest Gregor.

1002
01:58:05,167 --> 01:58:06,897
Nothing sir.

1003
01:58:10,319 --> 01:58:13,369
Sogut will smell blood and ash tonight.

1004
01:58:22,231 --> 01:58:27,131
The disorder emerging after the explosion
will open the gates of Sogut for us.

1005
01:58:28,179 --> 01:58:31,689
We'll flare up the fire with our swords
before it extinguishes.

1006
01:58:32,599 --> 01:58:34,729
Osman took my village from me.

1007
01:58:35,297 --> 01:58:38,917
I will take everything from him.

1008
01:58:39,996 --> 01:58:43,046
The Christian community will welcome us.

1009
01:58:43,294 --> 01:58:46,474
When they see us, they will say...

1010
01:58:47,354 --> 01:58:51,868
Here are the real owners of Christianity!
Our saviors!

1011
01:58:52,398 --> 01:58:54,748
It's about to get dark.

1012
01:59:05,541 --> 01:59:07,801
Brave sons of Byzantine!

1013
01:59:08,967 --> 01:59:13,647
We'll end the domination of Turks in
this land!

1014
01:59:16,068 --> 01:59:17,908
For Jesus!

1015
01:59:18,347 --> 01:59:19,907
For Caesar!

1016
01:59:20,059 --> 01:59:29,019
For Jesus! For Caesar!

1017
01:59:29,230 --> 01:59:31,360
Sogut.

1018
02:01:06,393 --> 02:01:09,233
When they tried to kill Gregor...

1019
02:01:09,926 --> 02:01:12,006
I shielded him!

1020
02:01:15,150 --> 02:01:17,810
I made him responsible for the
Christian community.

1021
02:01:19,513 --> 02:01:21,043
However...

1022
02:01:22,574 --> 02:01:24,944
...however how can he...

1023
02:01:26,560 --> 02:01:29,540
...do such a betrayal,
how can he be such an evil my Sheik?

1024
02:01:30,724 --> 02:01:35,474
The goodness and the badness of
a human cannot be observed.

1025
02:01:37,228 --> 02:01:38,998
You can't see from outside.

1026
02:01:39,514 --> 02:01:42,464
Everyone does what they deserve,
Osman Bey.

1027
02:01:44,503 --> 02:01:48,703
Priest's grudge is revealed.

1028
02:02:00,078 --> 02:02:01,878
Eyvallah my sheik.

1029
02:02:09,404 --> 02:02:11,034
Akca Dervish.

1030
02:02:11,923 --> 02:02:13,403
Is it time?

1031
02:02:13,457 --> 02:02:15,687
Yes Osman Bey.

1032
02:03:10,692 --> 02:03:13,352
Damn it, why does it not explode?

1033
02:03:40,190 --> 02:03:41,990
Ignoble dog!

1034
02:03:57,595 --> 02:03:59,595
No one is around.

1035
02:04:00,367 --> 02:04:01,837
It's weird.

1036
02:04:14,567 --> 02:04:16,187
Osman Bey.

1037
02:05:47,072 --> 02:05:48,192
Osman Bey...

1038
02:05:51,077 --> 02:05:52,857
I beg you to forgive me.

1039
02:05:57,152 --> 02:05:58,852
For God's sake.

1040
02:06:05,039 --> 02:06:06,459
Akca Dervish...

1041
02:06:08,393 --> 02:06:10,633
...was after you like a shadow.

1042
02:07:29,628 --> 02:07:31,148
I know...

1043
02:07:32,916 --> 02:07:35,646
...every step you had,
every plan you had with Lords.

1044
02:07:40,911 --> 02:07:43,791
But this is not the only thing I know.

1045
02:07:46,917 --> 02:07:49,097
There's also your cruelty!

1046
02:07:51,225 --> 02:07:54,745
Even your religion can't purify you!

1047
02:07:57,757 --> 02:08:00,377
Those shops you intended to burn...

1048
02:08:00,717 --> 02:08:02,707
...were sinlesses'.

1049
02:08:03,760 --> 02:08:06,470
Those houses you intended to burn...

1050
02:08:06,909 --> 02:08:08,609
...were innocents'.

1051
02:08:11,153 --> 02:08:13,593
The mosque you intended to burn...

1052
02:08:14,245 --> 02:08:16,385
...is the house of Muslims!

1053
02:08:25,959 --> 02:08:27,669
But you...

1054
02:08:33,986 --> 02:08:37,506
don't deserve Hadrat Isah (Jesus).

1055
02:08:40,938 --> 02:08:43,168
You are not different from Judas Iscariot!

1056
02:08:44,579 --> 02:08:49,839
You even betray your people for
your desires!

1057
02:09:30,624 --> 02:09:32,904
As long as Turks exist...

1058
02:09:38,682 --> 02:09:40,252
...we will bring justice...

1059
02:09:41,686 --> 02:09:44,546
... with our swords!

1060
02:09:48,017 --> 02:09:50,387
This is such a sword that...

1061
02:09:51,694 --> 02:09:56,034
...always cuts the cruels!

1062
02:10:03,941 --> 02:10:06,401
Do you have anything to say?

1063
02:10:14,648 --> 02:10:16,268
Mercy...

1064
02:10:17,050 --> 02:10:19,030
Mercy, Osman Bey.

1065
02:10:19,862 --> 02:10:21,198
Mercy.

1066
02:10:21,198 --> 02:10:23,308
Mercy to the cruel...

1067
02:10:25,135 --> 02:10:27,435
...is betrayal to the oppressed!

1068
02:10:50,371 --> 02:10:52,121
Now take him...

1069
02:10:52,910 --> 02:10:55,560
...to his dear friend Rogatus.

1070
02:10:56,546 --> 02:11:00,386
And you shall not come to my land again!

1071
02:11:22,816 --> 02:11:24,516
My judgement is based on...

1072
02:11:25,995 --> 02:11:28,335
...Allah's justice.

1073
02:11:30,080 --> 02:11:32,130
Priest Gregor...

1074
02:11:32,538 --> 02:11:37,998
...intended to kill everyone including
Muslims and non-Muslims.

1075
02:11:41,611 --> 02:11:45,731
We don't consider the religion
of this betrayer!

1076
02:11:46,825 --> 02:11:50,635
We kill him even
if the betrayer is a Muslim.

1077
02:11:54,317 --> 02:11:58,327
I am Osman Bey,
the son of Ertugrul Ghazi.

1078
02:11:59,932 --> 02:12:01,932
I won't differentiate my people.

1079
02:12:03,046 --> 02:12:05,426
I treat them all the same.

1080
02:12:06,514 --> 02:12:08,484
I judge with justice!

1081
02:12:08,531 --> 02:12:12,071
We are pleased with your judgement,
Osman Bey!

1082
02:12:13,043 --> 02:12:20,073
Long live Osman Bey!

1083
02:12:22,473 --> 02:12:26,753
Until the whole world is Turks' land...

1084
02:12:28,229 --> 02:12:31,809
...we will continue facing the cruels!

1085
02:12:32,739 --> 02:12:46,320
Long Live Osman Bey!

